{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"c5d4f185-9b12-442d-afa0-b138bfb601a0","title":"Local maximum and minimum of a cubic function"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c5d4f185-9b12-442d-afa0-b138bfb601a0","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Consider this cubic. A local maximum or minimum is a turning point, where the function changes between increasing and decreasing.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Local maxima and minima"},{"op":"equation","id":"function","region":"A2","latex":"f(x)=x^3-3x"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-2.2,2.2],"y":[-3.5,3.5],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"f(x)"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"cubic","y":"x^3-3*x","domain":[-2.1,2.1]}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c5d4f185-9b12-442d-afa0-b138bfb601a0","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Differentiate and set the slope equal to zero. The candidates are minus one and one, where the graph has horizontal tangents.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"derivative","anchor":{"el":"function","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(x)=3x^2-3=0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=\\pm1"},{"op":"figure","id":"candidates","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"peak","at":{"on":"cubic","x":-1},"label":"(−1, 2)"},{"kind":"point","id":"valley","at":{"on":"cubic","x":1},"label":"(1, −2)"},{"kind":"tangent","to":"cubic","x":-1,"length":0.25,"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"tangent","to":"cubic","x":1,"length":0.25,"stroke":"dashed"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"c5d4f185-9b12-442d-afa0-b138bfb601a0","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c5d4f185-9b12-442d-afa0-b138bfb601a0","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The derivative is positive outside these candidates and negative between them. Which candidate changes from increasing to decreasing?","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"signs","anchor":{"el":"derivative","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(x)>0\\text{ for }x<-1\\text{ or }x>1;\\quad f'(x)<0\\text{ for }-1<x<1"},{"op":"figure","id":"directions","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[-1.65,0.8],"text":"↗","size":"large"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.45,0.4],"text":"↘","size":"large"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.85,-0.9],"text":"↗","size":"large"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c5d4f185-9b12-442d-afa0-b138bfb601a0","step":{"id":"s4","script":"At minus one, rising becomes falling: a local maximum. At one, falling becomes rising: a local minimum. These are local, not global, extrema.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"classify","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[-1,3.05],"text":"local max"},{"kind":"text","at":[1,-3.05],"text":"local min"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"results","anchor":{"el":"signs","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\text{Local max: }f(-1)=2\\qquad\\text{Local min: }f(1)=-2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
